    "title": "GTA 6 Price Update Unites Gamers: \"Shut Up And Take My Money\"",
    "text": "Rockstar Games Published Mar 23, 2026, 8:00 PM EDT Austin King is the Senior Editor of Gaming at ScreenRant and has been with the site since 2020 with a focus on RPGs and tabletop games. He previously managed content for Geek to Geek Media, and has served as a writer for sites like Nintendad, Geek Fitness, and more. In addition to his work at ScreenRant, he also hosts the Dragon Quest FM podcast and is the author of several books, including co-writing Nimbus (a #1 bestseller in 2013). His latest is the nonfiction The Dragon Quest Book, available now. He's written about pop culture, video games, and genre studies over the course of his career. You can find him on BlueSky, X, and at Dragonquestaustin.com Sign in to your ScreenRant account Perhaps nothing regarding Grand Theft Auto 6 has been so heavily debated and speculated upon than its price. Even amidst nearly constant delay rumors, and a couple of trailers dropping, the price of GTA 6 has been a major talking point. Now, it looks like we may finally have some answers, and pretty much everyone seems thrilled. Over on Reddit, GTA fans discussed the news that Take-Two's CEO, Strauss Zelnick, indicated the price of the game will be between $70 and $80. This is more in-line with many AAA releases, so GTA 6 seemingly won't cost more just because it's such a massive and highly-anticipated game. Understandably, fans were pretty excited about this. GTA 6's Price Has Been Narrowed Down Massively It's best to take this with a grain of salt, however. In the interview, Zelnick didn't explicitly state this would be the price, but based around his comments, it seems like GTA 6 is targeting that $70–$80 price range Zelnick mentions: \"Very hard for me to believe that we would want to have interstitial advertising in a game that someone paid 70 or 80 bucks for. Would seem unfair.\" Presumably, this is about GTA 6, which is why fans are so excited. This Is Great News For GTA 6 Fans For years, GTA fans have thought they'd need to pay $100 or more for GTA 6, and while the cost of AAA games has risen in recent years, with $70 becoming the standard for many so-called premium releases, that's still a much better price than anything in the triple digits. Until a price is officially revealed for Grand Theft Auto 6, we won't know for sure, but this is hopefully a sign of a more affordable game being on the way. Released November 19, 2026 ESRB Rating Pending - Likely Mature 17+ Developer(s) Rockstar Games Publisher(s) Rockstar Games Engine Rockstar Advanced Game Engine (RAGE) Multiplayer Online Multiplayer",
